Description: Device Uniqueness Backend - Username Registration End to End
Network: ../zombienet-configs/local-dev.toml
Creds: config

# ============================================
# Prerequisites
# ============================================

people-collator1: is up

alice-paseo-validator: parachain 1502 is registered within 400 seconds
alice-paseo-validator: parachain 1502 block height is at least 5 within 500 seconds

# ============================================
# Registration
# ============================================

# Registers a fresh person and waits for the username to reach People Chain and
# the indexer's projection: challenge -> sr25519 proof -> JWT -> POST usernames
# -> outbox -> identity-chain-writer -> PeopleLite.attest -> search.
#
# Search going green is what makes this worth running. It is the only assertion
# that covers the writer's lease, the attestation allowance, the attester's
# signing key and finalization at once — a broken link anywhere leaves the
# reservation stuck in the outbox rather than failing loudly.
#
# The ring VRF key is real Bandersnatch material (verifiablejs), because
# PeopleLite::attest verifies proof_of_ownership against it; fabricated bytes
# are accepted by the API and rejected on chain with InvalidProofOfOwnership.
#
# Registers a random account each run, so it behaves the same against a genesis
# chain and a fork.
# 900s, larger than the script's own budget (300s readiness + 420s landing). The inner
# timeout has to be the one that fires: it reports which stage failed, whereas this one just
# says the script did not return in time.
people-collator1: js-script ./scripts/dist/test-dub-registration.js return is equal to 1 within 900 seconds
